  "source": "mcweed U66: 'on the bowl mold board, the holes are a bit too big and are overlapping, also two sections don't have holes' - a hole pattern laid out by its centres, never checked edge-wise against the feature it had to clear or against its neighbours.",
  "summary": "The bolt circle radius is derived, never given: the rule is stated edge-to-face, so it is bossOuterR + gap + holeR = 14 + 2 + 2.2 = 18.2, and the rim check 18.2 + 2.2 + 3 = 23.4 <= 30 has to be run before that radius is committed to. Two plausible misreadings: measuring to the hole's CENTRE gives 16.0 and drives the holes under the boss's footprint (that is the asfailed, caught by IoU, max_dev and eight probes), and using M4's nominal 4 mm instead of the 4.4 clearance diameter gives 18.0, which passes IoU and max_dev and is caught only by the two 0.2 mm edge probes at r = 20.3 and r = 15.9.",
  "expects_question": false,
